{"id": "EUVD-2026-101054", "enisaUuid": "4054924c-d14c-3769-99cc-61ef06d5670f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix missing iov bounds check in parse_posix_sids()\n\nIn parse_posix_sids(), sidsbuf_end is calculated using the server-supplied\nout_len without being validated against the actual length of the received\niov (iov_len).\n\nIf a server provides an inflated out_len, sidsbuf_end will point past the\nend of the iov. This defeats the bounds guards in posix_info_sid_size(),\nallowing out-of-bounds reads into adjacent kernel memory.\n\nFix this by rejecting responses where the calculated sidsbuf_end would\nexceed the received iov boundaries or cause pointer wraparound.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T13:42:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d91b9a3b2b38e5ac1b51e9e5b23fe53ad7b49644", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b862996e5105be1293da9cdc85da77b76021c3bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f8ed71aaaba3bc8b19cd9930cc62e63e142b299", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eac6917a42899aad0617bbf04798c5dd946a1fe5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b09d092eb24ad0110f16a9b7c1ed5d2a0c1733dc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gf4w-8ph4-r9fj", "CVE-2026-98405"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d136865-2c14-38f4-b641-1e4c28252087", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "858e74876c5cbff1dfd5bace99e32fbce2abd4b5 <b862996e5105be1293da9cdc85da77b76021c3bd"}, {"id": "1301ae3b-84b8-3698-acd2-63eea8c14967", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "858e74876c5cbff1dfd5bace99e32fbce2abd4b5 <eac6917a42899aad0617bbf04798c5dd946a1fe5"}, {"id": "34cfd127-9e44-31f0-b8a6-095bb78deb35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.32 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "37c78856-c915-3a0d-b00f-676b17a23b64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "402be113-3938-3606-a123-59cd338c448a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a90f37e3d7acfd9824f162830583bbf7846fe252 <d91b9a3b2b38e5ac1b51e9e5b23fe53ad7b49644"}, {"id": "44622d7d-965b-3409-8b91-c03d14fd46c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "858e74876c5cbff1dfd5bace99e32fbce2abd4b5 <b09d092eb24ad0110f16a9b7c1ed5d2a0c1733dc"}, {"id": "559871de-21ff-336a-a35a-dac3e99ca533", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "77927506-a16e-3eaa-84a6-7e34dc318c46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "b45f52a8-d900-39e3-981f-109af748f962", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "858e74876c5cbff1dfd5bace99e32fbce2abd4b5 <2f8ed71aaaba3bc8b19cd9930cc62e63e142b299"}, {"id": "c11f7967-9587-3c7c-be5d-3a00f1cd980f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "ca2ca7f1-000c-3ac4-a307-02460bcf4d16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d377f2b5-9978-3edb-be22-5a1bc88cdc8b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d442dc83-a037-3062-b42f-08e59e65b01c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "32d7fe50-3822-3721-907a-49cbfc60f867", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}